00:20:09.060 --> 00:20:13.040
NVIDIA builds three computers to enable developers to create physical AI.

333
00:20:13.660 --> 00:20:15.640
The models are first trained on DGX.

334
00:20:16.240 --> 00:20:21.980
Then, the AI is fine-tuned and tested using reinforcement learning physics feedback in Omniverse.

335
00:20:22.620 --> 00:20:27.480
And the trained AI runs on NVIDIA Jetson AGX robotics computers.

336
00:20:29.020 --> 00:20:34.040
NVIDIA Omniverse is a physics-based operating system for physical AI simulation.

337
00:20:34.040 --> 00:20:39.640
Robots learn and fine-tune their skills in Isaac Lab, a robot gym built on Omniverse.

338
00:20:40.120 --> 00:20:45.240
And with group workflows, like GroupGen, to generate diverse learning environments and layouts.

339
00:20:45.880 --> 00:20:52.040
GroupMimic, to generate large-scale synthetic motion data sets based on a small number of real-world captures.

340
00:20:52.040 --> 00:20:55.900
And group control for neural whole-body control.

341
00:20:57.300 --> 00:20:59.140
This is just one robot.

