00:20:59.740 --> 00:21:06.720
Future factories will orchestrate teams of robots and monitor entire operations through thousands of sensors.

343
00:21:08.000 --> 00:21:11.940
For factory digital twins, they use an Omniverse blueprint called MEGA.

344
00:21:11.940 --> 00:21:19.620
With MEGA, the factory digital twin is populated with virtual robots and their AI models, the robots' brains.

345
00:21:20.500 --> 00:21:28.660
The robots execute a task by perceiving their environment, reasoning, planning their next motion, and finally converting it to actions.

346
00:21:29.320 --> 00:21:33.760
These actions are simulated in the environment by the world simulator in Omniverse.

347
00:21:33.760 --> 00:21:38.340
And the results are perceived by the robot brains through Omniverse sensor simulation.

348
00:21:39.400 --> 00:21:44.720
Based on the sensor simulations, the robot brains decide the next action, and the loop continues.

349
00:21:45.160 --> 00:21:50.360
While MEGA precisely tracks the state and position of everything in the factory digital twin.

350
00:21:51.380 --> 00:21:57.740
This software-in-the-loop testing brings software-defined processes to physical spaces and embodiments.

351
00:21:57.740 --> 00:22:05.940
This is just letting industrial enterprises simulate and validate changes in an Omniverse digital twin before deploying to the physical world.

